From 5ecff7bb5230ff798cd08b020680e6338075531f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leoyzen <leoyzen@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 15:06:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [Quantization] Extend H200 [32,32] fp8_w8a8 tuned configs
 with more M buckets

The 7 existing H200 [32,32] block-FP8 tables only covered M=1 and M=2.
Extend them with M buckets 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 1024 and
2048 so the tuned kernel path is also selected for those batch sizes:

  - N=1152,K=5120
  - N=1792,K=5120
  - N=25600,K=6144
  - N=4096,K=1280
  - N=5120,K=2048
  - N=5120,K=576
  - N=8192,K=1280

The added tiers come from a local H200/L20X tuning sweep. L20X is the
OEM name of the same SM90 part as H200, so all tables are filed under
NVIDIA_H200. The M=1 and M=2 entries of the existing files are
unchanged.
---
